1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,955
Characters, actions, places, occupations, and events in this series are fictional and created for entertainment purposes only.

2
00:00:06,955 --> 00:00:10,903
They are not intended to urge or promote any behavior in the series.

3
00:00:10,903 --> 00:00:13,111
Viewer discretion is advised.

4
00:00:13,111 --> 00:00:14,971
Congrats, bro, on winning the basketball game.

5
00:00:14,971 --> 00:00:16,149
You’re getting way too cool.

6
00:00:16,349 --> 00:00:18,006
Why? Are you jealous, kid?

7
00:00:18,006 --> 00:00:19,246
If I’m allowed to be jealous, then I’m very jealous.

8
00:00:19,246 --> 00:00:21,230
Will P’Niran be Cheewa’s boyfriend?

9
00:00:22,428 --> 00:00:24,582
No matter how you end up feeling about me,

10
00:00:24,582 --> 00:00:26,252
I’ll still like you anyway.

11
00:00:26,385 --> 00:00:27,853
No matter then or now.

12
00:00:27,853 --> 00:00:30,159
Cheewa, what if I asked you back?

13
00:00:30,803 --> 00:00:31,956
Will you be my boyfriend?

14
00:00:32,711 --> 00:00:33,616
- Yes!
- Yes!

15
00:01:38,605 --> 00:01:41,014
Do you like him hitting on you?

16
00:01:48,138 --> 00:01:49,575
Did I ever turn him down?

17
00:01:55,355 --> 00:01:59,973
Cheewa and P’Niran.

18
00:02:03,657 --> 00:02:04,781
You kid…

19
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:09,277
Since we’re dating…

20
00:02:09,743 --> 00:02:10,769
Shall we get married?

21
00:02:10,769 --> 00:02:11,470
What?

22
00:02:13,426 --> 00:02:15,084
Why are you like this?

23
00:02:15,084 --> 00:02:16,559
Nerds aren’t like this.

24
00:02:16,825 --> 00:02:19,611
A nerd in love is like this.

25
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,662
But with you only, P’Niran.

26
00:02:23,193 --> 00:02:24,492
So we’re getting married?

27
00:02:24,492 --> 00:02:25,451
Don’t be ridiculous.

28
00:02:31,687 --> 00:02:33,727
I want to go to a wedding with you, P’Niran.

29
00:02:38,055 --> 00:02:38,742
Fine.

30
00:02:39,785 --> 00:02:40,672
Let’s go.

31
00:02:44,199 --> 00:02:48,503
Well… Let us tell you about how we met.

32
00:02:49,457 --> 00:02:51,003
Do you remember how we met?

33
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:54,638
I do.

34
00:02:54,949 --> 00:02:56,204
We met when…

35
00:02:56,204 --> 00:02:58,039
Niran’s mom is gorgeous.

36
00:02:58,594 --> 00:03:03,529
Why do you think her son is
as handsome as a god or an angel?

37
00:03:04,128 --> 00:03:06,114
You have a brother?

38
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,708
How does it feel that your mother
is getting remarried?

39
00:03:15,818 --> 00:03:17,492
Does it make you sad if I ask that?

40
00:03:17,714 --> 00:03:18,549
Am I allowed to ask?

41
00:03:22,632 --> 00:03:23,649
Of course, you are.

42
00:03:23,649 --> 00:03:24,492
I’m okay.

43
00:03:27,577 --> 00:03:28,920
I feel…

44
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:30,874
How should I say it?

45
00:03:31,163 --> 00:03:31,984
I don’t know.

46
00:03:32,605 --> 00:03:34,409
I’m just happy…

47
00:03:36,517 --> 00:03:38,260
I’m happy to see her happy.

48
00:03:38,571 --> 00:03:39,764
Yes.

49
00:03:39,764 --> 00:03:42,049
We hang out a lot and go out to dinner…

50
00:03:42,404 --> 00:03:44,255
Even though you don’t
live with her anymore?

51
00:03:47,007 --> 00:03:48,719
We stopped living together
a long time ago, didn’t we?

52
00:03:49,784 --> 00:03:51,600
Though I want to be with her forever,

53
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:54,996
but I understand.

54
00:03:56,749 --> 00:03:58,280
I feel like there is

55
00:03:58,746 --> 00:04:05,684
no one way of doing something.
It depends on your perspective.

56
00:04:06,328 --> 00:04:07,395
You’re right.

57
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:09,761
I still have so much to learn

58
00:04:10,516 --> 00:04:12,463
when it comes to handling changes like this.

59
00:04:13,573 --> 00:04:15,361
I think it’s all normal.

60
00:04:15,583 --> 00:04:17,779
I can’t say this from my own experience,

61
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,280
but you just gotta go with the flow.

62
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:21,440
Whatever happens happens.

63
00:04:21,573 --> 00:04:23,266
We’re not alone in the world, after all.

64
00:04:26,639 --> 00:04:28,810
I’m in your world, always.

65
00:04:33,848 --> 00:04:34,728
Umm.

66
00:04:36,592 --> 00:04:40,067
Are we… part of your world?

67
00:04:40,466 --> 00:04:41,181
Yeah.

68
00:04:45,902 --> 00:04:47,164
I guess that’s a no.

69
00:04:47,386 --> 00:04:48,911
It’s just the two of them
in their own little world.

70
00:04:50,420 --> 00:04:54,743
Thank you for all the presents,
especially the big ones.

71
00:04:54,743 --> 00:04:56,707
We’re really happy…

72
00:04:56,707 --> 00:05:00,056
We might be happier receiving your gifts
than we do getting married.

73
00:05:05,338 --> 00:05:07,044
Allow me to say this.

74
00:05:07,155 --> 00:05:10,668
I’m happy you’re all here today,

75
00:05:10,668 --> 00:05:19,509
but the guest who makes me the happiest
in the world, in the universe, for being here…

76
00:05:19,509 --> 00:05:20,615
Niran.

77
00:05:21,636 --> 00:05:26,194
My one and only beloved son.

78
00:05:26,594 --> 00:05:31,917
Please give Niran a round of applause
for being here for his mother today.

79
00:05:32,516 --> 00:05:33,993
Thank you, love.

80
00:05:37,569 --> 00:05:38,901
I love you.

81
00:05:45,795 --> 00:05:48,370
How lucky I am to get to be
at my mother’s wedding.

82
00:05:48,614 --> 00:05:50,323
You look really beautiful today, Mom.

83
00:05:50,656 --> 00:05:51,962
I’ll tell you what…

84
00:05:52,339 --> 00:05:56,146
I was just as beautiful at my first wedding.

85
00:05:56,146 --> 00:05:57,372
Oh, wow.

86
00:05:57,372 --> 00:05:59,383
I didn’t make it in time for that one.

87
00:05:59,672 --> 00:06:01,744
How’d I know if you’re not
just making it up, Mom?

88
00:06:02,143 --> 00:06:03,509
Too bad I didn’t get to see that
with my own eyes.

89
00:06:08,946 --> 00:06:09,910
Mom.

90
00:06:10,310 --> 00:06:11,037
Yes?

91
00:06:14,322 --> 00:06:15,948
I’m not single anymore.

92
00:06:18,792 --> 00:06:23,023
I’m happy you feel comfortable
telling me everything, Niran.

93
00:06:23,023 --> 00:06:25,836
I want to know all about you.

94
00:06:26,125 --> 00:06:30,000
Please tell me more one day, okay?

95
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:30,756
Of course.

96
00:06:37,014 --> 00:06:37,851
Niran.

97
00:06:39,294 --> 00:06:40,304
I…

98
00:06:41,502 --> 00:06:44,952
I’ll be the same old mom for you.

99
00:06:46,128 --> 00:06:46,920
Always.

100
00:06:49,361 --> 00:06:54,769
Please remember that I won’t ever love
anyone more than I love you.

101
00:06:57,210 --> 00:06:59,741
You’re my number one gold medalist.

102
00:07:07,414 --> 00:07:08,671
I know.

103
00:07:10,247 --> 00:07:14,944
I’m really happy we’re still just as close.

104
00:07:17,163 --> 00:07:19,475
Please live a happy life.

105
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:21,793
It will make me happy, too.

106
00:07:23,457 --> 00:07:25,315
Don’t worry about a thing on my end.

107
00:07:26,181 --> 00:07:27,821
I can take care of myself.

108
00:07:28,842 --> 00:07:30,611
And I have someone to help take care of me.

109
00:07:32,742 --> 00:07:33,804
Did you know, Mom…

110
00:07:33,804 --> 00:07:34,359
Hmm?

111
00:07:34,891 --> 00:07:37,859
There are millions of stars in this universe.

112
00:07:38,303 --> 00:07:40,214
I love you more than all of those.

113
00:07:43,210 --> 00:07:44,478
I love you, Mom.

114
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,143
Look at my Dad.

115
00:07:49,653 --> 00:07:50,959
Is he drunk?

116
00:07:53,422 --> 00:07:56,375
From my rough calculation, yes.

117
00:08:00,259 --> 00:08:05,531
Would you believe me if I said
I’d always been scared of this day.

118
00:08:06,663 --> 00:08:10,961
I prayed I would get so sick I couldn’t
make it to my mother’s wedding.

119
00:08:11,383 --> 00:08:13,963
So I wouldn’t have to see or hear anything.

120
00:08:15,184 --> 00:08:17,555
But now that I’m here…

121
00:08:20,994 --> 00:08:22,096
I’m still fine.

122
00:08:23,517 --> 00:08:28,061
On the other hand, I feel kinda relieved.

123
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,208
The future really is unexpected, huh?

124
00:08:32,940 --> 00:08:34,856
The world keeps turning and turning.

125
00:08:35,233 --> 00:08:38,464
So many things can happen within 24 hours.

126
00:08:39,680 --> 00:08:40,750
But at least,

127
00:08:41,867 --> 00:08:44,811
if there’s a day when I can smile
every once in a while,

128
00:08:45,566 --> 00:08:46,498
I’ll be okay with that.

129
00:08:49,383 --> 00:08:50,492
P’Niran.

130
00:08:52,778 --> 00:08:55,629
Did you know that back when
the dinosaurs walked the earth,

131
00:08:55,880 --> 00:08:58,920
the earth took only 22 hours
to revolve around itself?

132
00:08:59,053 --> 00:09:01,541
Like, is that a random fact
that just pops in your head?

133
00:09:02,828 --> 00:09:04,133
What I’m trying to say is that

134
00:09:04,488 --> 00:09:06,197
the world will keep moving
slower and slower.

135
00:09:06,863 --> 00:09:10,609
Every 100 years, a day lasts
1.7 milliseconds longer.

136
00:09:11,186 --> 00:09:14,392
In the future, a day will last 25 hours.

137
00:09:14,836 --> 00:09:15,493
Uh-huh.

138
00:09:16,292 --> 00:09:17,217
And?

139
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:21,732
No matter how many hours
there are in a day in the future,

140
00:09:22,930 --> 00:09:25,438
if there’s a day you can’t stand,

141
00:09:26,658 --> 00:09:28,132
please let me know.

142
00:09:29,153 --> 00:09:35,177
I’ll make sure the world turns more quickly
so your bad day passes by so fast.

143
00:09:37,862 --> 00:09:39,107
Can you do that?

144
00:09:39,862 --> 00:09:41,108
Make the world turn faster?

145
00:09:42,329 --> 00:09:44,902
Scientifically speaking, no.

146
00:09:56,728 --> 00:09:58,985
There are things science can’t do,

147
00:10:00,361 --> 00:10:01,490
but I can.

148
00:10:04,331 --> 00:10:05,514
Please wait and see.

149
00:10:11,843 --> 00:10:14,408
25 hours a day with you?

150
00:10:15,451 --> 00:10:16,260
I don’t want that.

151
00:10:19,456 --> 00:10:20,746
I want 30 hours.

152
00:10:27,426 --> 00:10:31,493
You know, when you say
something kind of nerdy,

153
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:34,089
it’s really adorable.

154
00:10:35,753 --> 00:10:37,021
I’m not nerdy.

155
00:10:38,774 --> 00:10:40,054
I’m in love.

156
00:10:50,075 --> 00:10:52,861
Just say you like him. Say it.

157
00:10:52,861 --> 00:10:54,275
Alright, in three, two, one.

158
00:10:54,564 --> 00:10:55,440
I like you.

159
00:10:57,082 --> 00:10:58,117
I like you, too.

160
00:10:59,626 --> 00:11:00,467
See?

161
00:11:02,720 --> 00:11:03,498
Thipok.

162
00:11:03,698 --> 00:11:04,424
Yeah?

163
00:11:04,646 --> 00:11:07,558
Congratulations on your label contract.

164
00:11:08,379 --> 00:11:10,634
Well… Are you into singers?

165
00:11:10,634 --> 00:11:11,440
Hmm.

166
00:11:12,727 --> 00:11:13,426
What are you even saying?

167
00:11:13,426 --> 00:11:14,136
You dummy.

168
00:11:14,358 --> 00:11:15,072
Bye!

169
00:11:24,737 --> 00:11:26,016
Thipok!

170
00:11:26,305 --> 00:11:27,556
Thipok.

171
00:11:27,867 --> 00:11:28,609
Thipok!

172
00:11:28,942 --> 00:11:29,862
Thipok!

173
00:11:31,621 --> 00:11:34,831
Handsome and cool.

174
00:11:35,452 --> 00:11:36,289
Niran.

175
00:11:38,908 --> 00:11:40,295
Look at you all.

176
00:11:40,295 --> 00:11:41,471
I’m not a ghost, you know?

177
00:11:44,711 --> 00:11:45,717
What now?

178
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:47,376
You’re messing with me again, huh?

179
00:11:56,833 --> 00:11:57,609
What?

180
00:12:02,197 --> 00:12:03,066
Hey, hey.

181
00:12:03,221 --> 00:12:03,979
Come on.

182
00:12:04,623 --> 00:12:05,295
Here.

183
00:12:05,428 --> 00:12:06,766
The biggest heart.

184
00:12:06,766 --> 00:12:07,830
For you.

185
00:12:12,735 --> 00:12:13,763
Thanks.

186
00:12:17,248 --> 00:12:19,871
Don’t miss me so much when we graduate.

187
00:12:21,247 --> 00:12:23,743
You’re the one who’s gonna miss me.

188
00:12:24,409 --> 00:12:26,878
It’s going to be lonely without
someone to pick a fight with.

189
00:12:30,163 --> 00:12:31,080
You dummy…

190
00:12:34,342 --> 00:12:35,171
See you.

191
00:12:40,266 --> 00:12:40,987
Oy.

192
00:12:41,853 --> 00:12:43,128
You can punch me in the face.

193
00:12:43,439 --> 00:12:44,819
I’ll hold you to that.

194
00:12:46,794 --> 00:12:47,793
Go on.

195
00:12:48,503 --> 00:12:49,344
See you.

196
00:13:00,195 --> 00:13:01,368
Where’s mine?

197
00:13:02,766 --> 00:13:03,833
You want a heart?

198
00:13:04,277 --> 00:13:07,030
I think this is gonna be a long talk.

199
00:13:07,274 --> 00:13:09,104
Someone’s in trouble.

200
00:13:10,702 --> 00:13:11,848
- Let’s scram, guys.
- What do you need it for?

201
00:13:12,413 --> 00:13:13,762
You have so many.

202
00:13:15,693 --> 00:13:16,485
Ugh.

203
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:26,152
P’Niran.

204
00:13:31,888 --> 00:13:32,470
What?

205
00:13:32,470 --> 00:13:33,198
What are you doing?

206
00:13:39,738 --> 00:13:41,749
You really can’t let Oy win, can you?

207
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:46,101
A feeling called jealousy arose.

208
00:13:47,854 --> 00:13:49,590
You were jealous of me with Oy?

209
00:13:50,855 --> 00:13:52,376
I’d still be jealous if it was anyone else.

210
00:13:53,685 --> 00:13:56,891
If someone gives you a sticker
bigger than mine,

211
00:13:58,067 --> 00:13:59,604
please call me.

212
00:14:00,270 --> 00:14:03,898
I’ll have a bigger one printed.

213
00:14:06,583 --> 00:14:07,765
Okay. Got it.

214
00:14:08,919 --> 00:14:09,985
Go to class.

215
00:14:09,985 --> 00:14:11,000
I have to go, too.

216
00:14:12,465 --> 00:14:13,613
Okay.

217
00:14:16,076 --> 00:14:16,817
Let’s go, guys.

218
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:20,534
My heart has to be the biggest, P’Niran.

219
00:14:29,665 --> 00:14:30,789
I know that.

220
00:14:33,474 --> 00:14:34,752
I don’t care about anyone else’s heart,

221
00:14:36,572 --> 00:14:37,607
only yours.

222
00:14:42,601 --> 00:14:43,827
It’s been like that for a while now, too.

223
00:14:44,581 --> 00:14:45,314
You happy, now?

224
00:14:51,615 --> 00:14:54,925
You have to ask everyone
if they’re happy now.

225
00:14:55,502 --> 00:14:56,602
- Yes.
- Yes.

226
00:14:57,223 --> 00:14:58,192
Thank you.

227
00:14:59,723 --> 00:15:01,296
I’m happy, too.

228
00:15:05,646 --> 00:15:06,815
I think we should get going.

229
00:15:08,746 --> 00:15:10,195
Let’s be proper students.

230
00:15:12,192 --> 00:15:13,014
I have to go.

231
00:15:19,118 --> 00:15:20,906
Can you guys see my big heart?

232
00:15:51,502 --> 00:15:53,486
Let’s try jamming with the band.

233
00:15:54,631 --> 00:15:55,527
Hey, guys.

234
00:15:55,527 --> 00:15:57,074
This is Cheewa,

235
00:15:57,074 --> 00:15:58,349
the kid I asked to be on the drum.

236
00:15:58,349 --> 00:16:00,407
You brought a nerd to be our drummer?

237
00:16:00,407 --> 00:16:00,936
Yeah.

238
00:16:00,936 --> 00:16:02,401
The drum sets the beat for the song, dude.

239
00:16:02,510 --> 00:16:04,777
I don’t think this glasses-guy
even walks straight.

240
00:16:09,756 --> 00:16:10,814
Were you guys…

241
00:16:13,122 --> 00:16:14,619
amazing musicians fresh out of the womb?

242
00:16:16,691 --> 00:16:18,909
We’re just being funny.

243
00:16:19,200 --> 00:16:20,550
Come on now.

244
00:16:20,823 --> 00:16:22,710
These two just love running their mouths.

245
00:16:22,710 --> 00:16:23,459
Don’t take it seriously.

246
00:16:23,731 --> 00:16:24,876
You guys, come on.

247
00:16:24,876 --> 00:16:25,715
Just pack up and leave.

248
00:16:25,715 --> 00:16:26,602
If you’re done, just go.

249
00:16:26,602 --> 00:16:27,460
It’s okay, P’Niran.

250
00:16:30,295 --> 00:16:31,339
Shall we begin?

251
00:16:31,721 --> 00:16:32,808
Oh, hey, Cheewa.

252
00:16:33,662 --> 00:16:34,885
For the Farewell Day,

253
00:16:35,158 --> 00:16:38,052
can you be on the drum in my friend’s place?

254
00:16:38,052 --> 00:16:38,658
What?

255
00:16:38,922 --> 00:16:40,409
You want Cheewa to play the drum?

256
00:16:41,082 --> 00:16:42,130
Do you know how to play the drums?

257
00:16:53,416 --> 00:16:54,744
Are you good at everything, Cheewa?

258
00:16:54,744 --> 00:16:55,909
How come you can do everything?

259
00:16:55,909 --> 00:16:57,611
Is there anything you can’t do?

260
00:16:58,429 --> 00:16:59,483
There’s plenty of them.

261
00:16:59,665 --> 00:17:01,258
Of course I can’t do everything.

262
00:17:03,021 --> 00:17:03,749
But…

263
00:17:04,094 --> 00:17:06,600
The Farewell Day is for you and your friends,

264
00:17:06,981 --> 00:17:08,301
so I want to do my best.

265
00:17:09,192 --> 00:17:10,783
If it’s something that has to do with you,

266
00:17:11,492 --> 00:17:12,437
I’ll do it.

267
00:17:15,291 --> 00:17:17,030
You’re such a sweet talker now, Cheewa.

268
00:17:17,139 --> 00:17:18,654
You won’t want any other dessert.

269
00:17:19,454 --> 00:17:20,650
I’ll be your only source of sugar.

270
00:17:23,794 --> 00:17:24,723
Are you hungry?

271
00:17:26,304 --> 00:17:27,868
If you are, I can be.

272
00:17:28,577 --> 00:17:31,136
I need something sweet, too.

273
00:17:31,645 --> 00:17:33,358
You’re never sweet to me at all.

274
00:17:35,703 --> 00:17:38,317
P’Thipok, can you please behave?

275
00:17:39,262 --> 00:17:41,195
Come on, Newton.

276
00:17:41,304 --> 00:17:44,567
It’s just the year book,
not a visa application.

277
00:17:44,567 --> 00:17:45,884
There’s no need to be so strict.

278
00:17:45,957 --> 00:17:46,636
Fine.

279
00:17:46,636 --> 00:17:47,774
I’ll take the photo now.

280
00:17:47,956 --> 00:17:49,649
One, two, three.

281
00:17:50,249 --> 00:17:51,724
All done.

282
00:17:51,888 --> 00:17:53,046
Oh, Newton.

283
00:17:53,137 --> 00:17:55,217
Are you a full-time photographer now?

284
00:17:55,435 --> 00:17:57,002
You’re not after the aliens anymore?

285
00:17:57,002 --> 00:18:00,712
Oh, the audio-visual teacher has to set up
the sound system at the auditorium,

286
00:18:00,712 --> 00:18:02,630
so I was asked to be the photographer
for the year book for today.

287
00:18:02,630 --> 00:18:04,231
Where are Cheewa and Jomyut?

288
00:18:05,049 --> 00:18:08,465
I think they’re also preparing for
the Farewell Day at the auditorium.

289
00:18:08,629 --> 00:18:09,779
I was told they’re freaking tired.

290
00:18:09,779 --> 00:18:10,279
Oh?

291
00:18:12,642 --> 00:18:14,944
Since when did you swear like that?

292
00:18:15,198 --> 00:18:16,330
You’ve become a rascal.

293
00:18:16,475 --> 00:18:17,848
You must have spent too much
time with Hem.

294
00:18:17,848 --> 00:18:18,457
Here.

295
00:18:20,383 --> 00:18:21,147
Thank you.

296
00:18:22,001 --> 00:18:23,053
For Cheewa.

297
00:18:23,526 --> 00:18:24,270
Oh.

298
00:18:24,597 --> 00:18:25,490
It’s for Cheewa?

299
00:18:25,690 --> 00:18:26,324
Umm.

300
00:18:27,869 --> 00:18:28,523
Okay.

301
00:18:28,523 --> 00:18:29,634
I’ll pass it on to him.

302
00:18:29,797 --> 00:18:30,554
Thanks.

303
00:18:32,499 --> 00:18:33,726
Go on with your job.

304
00:18:33,922 --> 00:18:35,330
I never get anything like that.

305
00:18:36,184 --> 00:18:37,278
Don’t you eat it.

306
00:18:37,442 --> 00:18:38,416
Put it in your pocket.

307
00:18:38,416 --> 00:18:38,922
Of course.

308
00:18:39,722 --> 00:18:40,495
I’ll keep it safe.

309
00:18:40,495 --> 00:18:41,636
You never give us anything like that.

310
00:18:42,435 --> 00:18:43,542
Ready?

311
00:18:44,215 --> 00:18:46,036
One, two, three.

312
00:18:46,227 --> 00:18:47,466
I just want this one.

313
00:18:47,811 --> 00:18:48,913
No need to bring more.

314
00:18:49,040 --> 00:18:50,257
Cheewa isn’t here?

315
00:18:50,802 --> 00:18:52,095
He’s still in the student council’s room.

316
00:18:53,295 --> 00:18:54,574
P’Niran asked me to pass this on to him.

317
00:18:54,574 --> 00:18:55,747
You can leave it with me.

318
00:18:55,747 --> 00:18:57,363
I have to be back at the
student council’s room anyway.

319
00:18:57,363 --> 00:18:58,219
Alright.

320
00:19:00,455 --> 00:19:01,922
Make sure it’s symmetrical.

321
00:19:02,376 --> 00:19:04,638
Yes, the two of them.

322
00:19:05,941 --> 00:19:06,905
Isn’t Cheewa here?

323
00:19:07,287 --> 00:19:09,943
I believe he’s gone back to the
auditorium to grab some stuff.

324
00:19:09,943 --> 00:19:12,346
But he has to be back to debrief with
the teacher here anyway.

325
00:19:12,855 --> 00:19:13,649
Okay.

326
00:19:13,776 --> 00:19:16,369
Can you pass this on to him?

327
00:19:16,714 --> 00:19:17,956
It’s a little something sweet from P’Niran.

328
00:19:17,956 --> 00:19:18,738
Of course.

329
00:19:24,387 --> 00:19:25,490
Oh, you guys.

330
00:19:26,908 --> 00:19:28,354
Good thing you’re here.

331
00:19:28,463 --> 00:19:30,037
Can you come and help me
carry some stuff?

332
00:19:32,891 --> 00:19:34,024
Honestly?

333
00:19:34,442 --> 00:19:35,945
Law school?

334
00:19:37,108 --> 00:19:37,828
Yes.

335
00:19:37,828 --> 00:19:39,623
I just realized I want to be a lawyer.

336
00:19:41,495 --> 00:19:43,287
I’m surprised.

337
00:19:43,287 --> 00:19:44,668
My dad said the same thing.

338
00:19:44,923 --> 00:19:46,595
Who’d have thought, right, Coach?

339
00:19:46,722 --> 00:19:47,610
Look at his face.

340
00:19:48,373 --> 00:19:49,048
What?

341
00:19:49,048 --> 00:19:50,114
What do you mean?

342
00:19:50,114 --> 00:19:51,150
What’s wrong with my face?

343
00:19:51,386 --> 00:19:52,469
You’re cute, buddy.

344
00:19:54,105 --> 00:19:55,303
You’re respectable.

345
00:19:55,303 --> 00:19:56,429
Oh…

346
00:19:58,447 --> 00:19:59,656
What about you, Niran?

347
00:19:59,656 --> 00:20:00,383
What do you want to study?

348
00:20:06,376 --> 00:20:08,216
I’m not sure, Coach.

349
00:20:08,922 --> 00:20:10,585
Honestly,

350
00:20:12,748 --> 00:20:15,020
I don’t want to stop playing judo,

351
00:20:15,020 --> 00:20:18,157
but I’m not sure about a lot of things.

352
00:20:25,525 --> 00:20:28,433
The Judo Club will still be here.

353
00:20:29,051 --> 00:20:30,226
It’s not going anywhere.

354
00:20:30,571 --> 00:20:32,154
When you want a place to come back to,

355
00:20:32,954 --> 00:20:33,885
you’re always welcomed.

356
00:20:40,956 --> 00:20:44,112
Soon enough Thara
will be your lawyer, Coach.

357
00:20:44,112 --> 00:20:44,853
What?

358
00:20:46,325 --> 00:20:47,000
Definitely.

359
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:48,819
Hello, Mr. Lawyer.

360
00:20:48,819 --> 00:20:49,534
That’s right.

361
00:20:49,534 --> 00:20:50,402
I’m going to be a lawyer.

362
00:20:50,402 --> 00:20:51,256
What kind of lawyer?

363
00:20:51,584 --> 00:20:53,513
I don’t know that, but I’ll be a lawyer.

364
00:20:53,840 --> 00:20:55,008
Oh, you.

365
00:21:12,780 --> 00:21:13,533
Where is he?

366
00:21:19,913 --> 00:21:20,896
Ugh.

367
00:21:21,732 --> 00:21:23,045
What should I do with my life?

368
00:21:25,208 --> 00:21:26,718
Cheewa isn’t here for me to talk to as well.

369
00:21:28,813 --> 00:21:30,035
What did you say about me?

370
00:21:44,878 --> 00:21:46,864
Newton really did hand it
to you himself, huh?

371
00:21:47,155 --> 00:21:49,179
Oh, Cheewa, there you are.

372
00:21:49,433 --> 00:21:51,252
P’Niran asked me to give you some candy,

373
00:21:51,252 --> 00:21:52,540
but I left it with Jomyut.

374
00:21:52,540 --> 00:21:54,018
Where is Jomyut?

375
00:21:54,018 --> 00:21:56,263
He said he’d see you at
the student council’s room.

376
00:22:01,025 --> 00:22:01,936
Oh, Cheewa.

377
00:22:02,554 --> 00:22:04,104
I got the wrong box.

378
00:22:04,104 --> 00:22:05,029
Help me out.

379
00:22:05,029 --> 00:22:05,651
Yes.

380
00:22:10,377 --> 00:22:11,402
Please go on ahead, sir.

381
00:22:11,402 --> 00:22:12,358
I’ll be right behind you.

382
00:22:12,639 --> 00:22:13,139
Oh?

383
00:22:14,320 --> 00:22:14,974
Okay.

384
00:22:21,899 --> 00:22:22,855
The candy took a long journey.

385
00:22:27,527 --> 00:22:29,182
What are you worrying about?

386
00:22:30,691 --> 00:22:31,756
Well…

387
00:22:32,629 --> 00:22:33,377
Same old stuff.

388
00:22:33,577 --> 00:22:34,699
University?

389
00:22:35,481 --> 00:22:36,436
Umm.

390
00:22:38,526 --> 00:22:40,784
I went to see Coach Ong today.

391
00:22:41,547 --> 00:22:42,669
I wanted to thank him, really.

392
00:22:44,069 --> 00:22:46,009
But when he asked me
what I want to go on studying,

393
00:22:47,354 --> 00:22:49,524
I felt like I was asked if
I’d continue playing judo.

394
00:22:50,851 --> 00:22:52,366
Well, I…

395
00:22:55,638 --> 00:22:56,833
I don’t know.

396
00:22:56,833 --> 00:22:58,542
I don’t know what I’m saying.

397
00:23:03,575 --> 00:23:04,807
Please take your time.

398
00:23:06,098 --> 00:23:07,952
You don’t need to have
an answer right away.

399
00:23:13,360 --> 00:23:14,544
How could I not?

400
00:23:15,126 --> 00:23:16,604
I have to submit an application this Friday.

401
00:23:19,112 --> 00:23:21,073
You have your whole life
ahead of you, P’Niran.

402
00:23:21,218 --> 00:23:22,352
Not just till Friday.

403
00:23:25,223 --> 00:23:31,680
Don’t let a single question or opinion
rush you into making a decision.

404
00:23:36,878 --> 00:23:39,982
Except… when I asked you
to be my boyfriend.

405
00:23:43,654 --> 00:23:45,985
Please don’t take it as me pressuring you.

406
00:23:50,838 --> 00:23:51,460
Cheewa.

407
00:23:54,368 --> 00:23:55,736
Do you want me to keep playing judo?

408
00:23:57,208 --> 00:23:59,159
I want you to be happy.

409
00:24:02,812 --> 00:24:04,034
Did I ask the wrong question or what?

410
00:24:05,852 --> 00:24:06,904
It was correct.

411
00:24:07,976 --> 00:24:10,237
I just want you to do
whatever makes you happy.

412
00:24:12,128 --> 00:24:13,901
Whatever you decide to do,

413
00:24:14,101 --> 00:24:15,618
I’m going to be cheering you on.

414
00:24:17,054 --> 00:24:18,680
Please don’t pressure yourself.

415
00:24:22,733 --> 00:24:24,231
You’re spoiling me.

416
00:24:26,394 --> 00:24:27,994
Are you happy if you’re spoiled?

417
00:24:29,484 --> 00:24:31,042
If so, please be spoiled.

418
00:24:32,187 --> 00:24:33,646
I like you either way.

419
00:24:44,878 --> 00:24:46,695
Please look up at the sky.

420
00:24:49,294 --> 00:24:51,587
It will make thinking feel much easier.

421
00:24:59,415 --> 00:25:01,288
Kissing also makes you feel relaxed.

422
00:25:01,888 --> 00:25:02,995
Did you know that?

423
00:25:04,758 --> 00:25:06,623
Maybe, after we do that,

424
00:25:07,186 --> 00:25:11,513
you might even come up with
what to do with your future right away.

425
00:25:15,603 --> 00:25:16,555
Shall we do it now?

426
00:25:16,973 --> 00:25:18,225
So you can make a decision by Friday.

427
00:25:40,336 --> 00:25:41,058
You’re funny.

428
00:25:43,530 --> 00:25:44,803
Look at you.

429
00:25:46,002 --> 00:25:47,227
You’re a big nerd.

430
00:25:47,609 --> 00:25:48,964
Where did you learn all this from?

431
00:25:52,981 --> 00:25:54,490
I read a lot of novels.

432
00:25:54,744 --> 00:25:55,244
You do?

433
00:25:57,043 --> 00:25:58,398
I guess I know the book.

434
00:26:05,826 --> 00:26:10,080
I really say everything from my heart.

435
00:26:10,716 --> 00:26:14,389
Bon voyage and good luck.

436
00:26:25,713 --> 00:26:28,071
School isn’t just a second home.

437
00:26:28,452 --> 00:26:29,531
Do you know what it is?

438
00:26:30,474 --> 00:26:31,723
Does anyone know?

439
00:26:33,167 --> 00:26:34,186
That’s right.

440
00:26:34,402 --> 00:26:36,012
It’s not just a second home,

441
00:26:36,112 --> 00:26:41,032
but a third, fourth, fifth,
maybe not a sixth.

442
00:26:41,350 --> 00:26:43,253
That would be too many homes.

443
00:26:47,420 --> 00:26:51,269
I hope you all go out there and live a full life.

444
00:26:51,651 --> 00:26:53,205
Don’t forget this home.

445
00:26:53,205 --> 00:26:56,184
This place will welcome you home
whenever you miss it.

446
00:27:11,211 --> 00:27:16,459
Hello, directors, teachers,
and all Grade 12 students.

447
00:27:16,954 --> 00:27:18,581
My name is Parncheewa.

448
00:27:19,112 --> 00:27:22,414
I represent the student council
in wishing you all good luck.

449
00:27:23,925 --> 00:27:25,484
FAREWELL DAY
I’m not good with words.

450
00:27:26,214 --> 00:27:28,417
I might even sound too blunt at times.

451
00:27:29,894 --> 00:27:34,201
But I really say everything from my heart.

452
00:27:44,128 --> 00:27:50,830
I believe one of the first big decisions
a person makes is choosing a university.

453
00:27:51,514 --> 00:27:55,510
We have to analyze our own skills, interests,

454
00:27:55,693 --> 00:27:59,725
and even foresee
how we will be in the future.

455
00:28:00,273 --> 00:28:05,083
It’s like shooting for the star in the sky.

456
00:28:05,474 --> 00:28:10,677
But did you know that light travels
at 300,000 kilometers per second?

457
00:28:11,407 --> 00:28:14,450
- Pay attention! Cheewa is talking.
- If a star is 100 light-years away from us…

458
00:28:15,081 --> 00:28:19,344
…it means light takes 100 years to reach us.

459
00:28:19,626 --> 00:28:22,221
In simple terms, that star no longer exists.

460
00:28:22,536 --> 00:28:24,390
We see what’s from 100 years ago.

461
00:28:24,838 --> 00:28:27,540
When the light from that star reaches us,

462
00:28:27,723 --> 00:28:31,771
the stars might have burst
or burned out a long time ago.

463
00:28:41,464 --> 00:28:44,040
What a guy from the Astrology Club
like me is trying to say is that

464
00:28:44,820 --> 00:28:46,855
there is no need for you
to look for yourself in the sky.

465
00:28:47,785 --> 00:28:50,989
Who you are and where you are right now

466
00:28:51,404 --> 00:28:54,293
is already beautiful and shining brightly
as you should be.

467
00:28:54,492 --> 00:28:57,653
We are all living stars and present.

468
00:28:58,367 --> 00:29:02,056
We have dreams, hopes, and courage.

469
00:29:02,654 --> 00:29:06,382
I’m rooting for all of you Grade 12 students
to become new stars,

470
00:29:06,631 --> 00:29:08,532
ones where you make yourselves

471
00:29:09,047 --> 00:29:11,577
and put in the universe all on your own.

472
00:29:13,021 --> 00:29:16,030
Bon voyage and good luck.

473
00:29:17,092 --> 00:29:19,620
I will watch your shining light from right here.

474
00:29:19,985 --> 00:29:20,735
Thank you.

475
00:29:34,200 --> 00:29:36,019
I love you, bud!

476
00:29:37,579 --> 00:29:39,406
I love you all so much.

477
00:29:39,406 --> 00:29:41,431
Don’t forget about me.

478
00:29:43,804 --> 00:29:46,183
I don’t want to graduate.

479
00:29:47,057 --> 00:29:48,330
I don’t want to work.

480
00:29:48,330 --> 00:29:50,988
I don’t want to study and work
at the same time.

481
00:29:50,988 --> 00:29:52,743
I don’t want to study, either.

482
00:29:52,743 --> 00:29:55,474
I want to work. I don’t want to study!

483
00:29:57,840 --> 00:29:59,133
You’re hurting me!

484
00:29:59,133 --> 00:30:00,529
I love you, too!

485
00:30:00,728 --> 00:30:01,757
Thank you.

486
00:30:02,549 --> 00:30:04,070
Thank you.

487
00:30:04,286 --> 00:30:06,124
Thank you.

488
00:30:07,048 --> 00:30:08,505
Thank you.

489
00:30:27,248 --> 00:30:28,859
One, two, three.

490
00:30:37,462 --> 00:30:38,509
Your speech was touching.

491
00:30:38,758 --> 00:30:41,039
I didn’t know you could be like that, Cheewa.

492
00:30:42,433 --> 00:30:44,447
I don’t look it, but I’m actually a romantic.

493
00:30:45,626 --> 00:30:46,157
You are?

494
00:30:46,489 --> 00:30:47,516
You’re a romantic?

495
00:30:48,977 --> 00:30:49,995
Why are you making fun of me?

496
00:30:50,991 --> 00:30:53,210
I’ve been like that with you all this time.

497
00:30:55,866 --> 00:30:57,873
I didn’t say I don’t believe you.

498
00:31:01,276 --> 00:31:02,990
Do you like it when I’m romantic?

499
00:31:04,799 --> 00:31:08,551
If you do, I’ll keep doing it.

500
00:31:10,112 --> 00:31:11,009
Oh, you…

501
00:31:11,905 --> 00:31:13,007
You’re more talkative than I am

502
00:31:13,671 --> 00:31:15,046
and then tell people
you’re not good with words.

503
00:31:15,474 --> 00:31:17,357
I’m only talkative with you, P’Niran.

504
00:31:18,901 --> 00:31:20,092
I don’t talk to other people.

505
00:31:26,500 --> 00:31:27,574
So what did you write?

506
00:31:30,304 --> 00:31:31,123
Please take a guess.

507
00:31:31,980 --> 00:31:38,349
(Parncheewa loves P’Niran.)

508
00:31:39,959 --> 00:31:40,728
Am I right?

509
00:31:50,404 --> 00:31:51,902
Please keep it between us.

510
00:31:56,650 --> 00:31:58,011
There’s just the two of us here.

511
00:31:58,360 --> 00:31:59,310
No one will know.

512
00:32:05,640 --> 00:32:06,388
P’Niran.

513
00:32:07,550 --> 00:32:08,178
Yeah?

514
00:32:09,622 --> 00:32:13,823
I know I said, ‘Bon voyage,’

515
00:32:15,798 --> 00:32:18,066
but please don’t walk too far away from me.

516
00:32:19,875 --> 00:32:20,680
What do you mean?

517
00:32:21,444 --> 00:32:23,337
Don’t fall for anyone on campus.

518
00:32:24,354 --> 00:32:25,999
I don’t even know if
I’d ever get into any school.

519
00:32:27,825 --> 00:32:28,626
Whatever.

520
00:32:29,157 --> 00:32:30,398
Please wait for me.

521
00:32:31,427 --> 00:32:33,246
Please don’t fall out of my orbit.

522
00:32:35,553 --> 00:32:36,899
Wanna just go to university together?

523
00:32:48,067 --> 00:32:49,716
We’ll walk hand in hand,

524
00:32:51,691 --> 00:32:53,277
and take our first leap together.

525
00:32:54,406 --> 00:32:55,270
What do you think?

526
00:32:58,922 --> 00:32:59,764
I like it.

527
00:33:00,262 --> 00:33:03,614
We’ll go together
and explore the universe together.

528
00:33:11,788 --> 00:33:13,190
Let’s go.

529
00:33:18,270 --> 00:33:19,914
Whatever star you’re aiming for,

530
00:33:20,694 --> 00:33:22,455
I’ll be the one to take you there.

531
00:33:24,596 --> 00:33:25,883
I promised you.

532
00:33:27,045 --> 00:33:28,560
I am a man of my word.

533
00:33:30,884 --> 00:33:34,348
You sure you really know
how to ride a spaceship?

534
00:33:35,474 --> 00:33:37,492
Just come along with me.

535
00:33:46,598 --> 00:33:47,950
Your future…

536
00:33:50,307 --> 00:33:51,712
Please leave it with me.

537
00:33:58,144 --> 00:34:01,262
Your whole body is gonna turn red
from all the blushing.

538
00:34:06,425 --> 00:34:07,362
Parncheewa, you…

539
00:34:07,627 --> 00:34:08,301
Come on.

540
00:34:36,064 --> 00:34:37,993
(When you stand right
in front of me like this,)

541
00:34:38,889 --> 00:34:43,250
(you shine brighter than any stars, Cheewa.)

542
00:35:03,610 --> 00:35:07,124
If it’s not gravity, it must be destiny.

543
00:35:29,840 --> 00:35:33,595
Gravity brought the bride
and the groom together.

544
00:35:43,271 --> 00:35:48,420
I used to believe that gravity is
the pulling force between two masses.

545
00:35:48,884 --> 00:35:52,827
But as I grew older, I’ve come to learn
about the theory that goes:

546
00:35:53,958 --> 00:35:56,177
Gravity might not actually be a force,

547
00:35:57,085 --> 00:36:02,895
but a bend in space and time.

548
00:36:10,504 --> 00:36:11,361
Cheewa.

549
00:36:11,482 --> 00:36:13,729
That might be too complicated.

550
00:36:15,929 --> 00:36:16,622
Uh…

551
00:36:17,894 --> 00:36:19,377
Allow me to redo it.

552
00:36:20,951 --> 00:36:22,128
My father…

553
00:36:23,763 --> 00:36:26,233
Actually he is the father of…

554
00:36:27,969 --> 00:36:29,735
Someone I love and adore.

555
00:36:30,684 --> 00:36:33,735
He found love again in his 50’s.

556
00:36:34,300 --> 00:36:37,526
He left home roughly three times a week.

557
00:36:37,526 --> 00:36:39,313
…Cheewa’s gonna be here soon.

558
00:36:39,373 --> 00:36:42,461
He went to the hospital only once
for the first time in so many years,

559
00:36:42,925 --> 00:36:45,118
but still met the bride.

560
00:36:49,975 --> 00:36:51,134
It’s destiny.

561
00:36:52,607 --> 00:36:56,364
If it’s not gravity, it must be destiny.

562
00:36:57,353 --> 00:37:00,368
Congratulations you found each other.

563
00:37:18,152 --> 00:37:19,942
Did I make any sense just now?

564
00:37:20,407 --> 00:37:21,333
I was so nervous.

565
00:37:23,149 --> 00:37:24,235
Take it easy.

566
00:37:24,396 --> 00:37:25,884
Nobody says anything, okay?

567
00:37:26,146 --> 00:37:27,504
Your speech is so much better than mine.

568
00:37:34,591 --> 00:37:35,667
I…

569
00:37:38,694 --> 00:37:40,246
I don’t know what to say.

570
00:37:43,435 --> 00:37:44,520
Except…

571
00:37:49,203 --> 00:37:50,228
I love you, Dad.

572
00:37:59,326 --> 00:38:00,188
Congratulations.

573
00:38:06,312 --> 00:38:07,242
Free hug.

574
00:38:08,877 --> 00:38:10,124
Always free for you, Dad.

575
00:38:10,407 --> 00:38:11,698
Congratulations.

576
00:38:14,708 --> 00:38:15,913
It wasn’t good.

577
00:38:17,066 --> 00:38:18,784
I confused everyone.

578
00:38:21,145 --> 00:38:22,413
Why are you laughing?

579
00:38:22,514 --> 00:38:24,341
It’s your father’s wedding.

580
00:38:27,046 --> 00:38:28,970
Why did you ask me to make a speech?

581
00:38:29,353 --> 00:38:34,222
You know I wouldn’t make sense
to people if I did.

582
00:38:35,716 --> 00:38:36,758
I just want to show you off.

583
00:38:37,182 --> 00:38:37,899
That’s all.

584
00:38:42,077 --> 00:38:44,456
I love hearing you talk about what you love.

585
00:38:44,900 --> 00:38:46,027
You look so special when you do.

586
00:38:47,077 --> 00:38:51,523
I just want everyone to know
how smart my boyfriend is.

587
00:38:58,526 --> 00:39:00,452
You’re making me blush.

588
00:39:03,674 --> 00:39:06,361
You’re the smartest person in the universe.

589
00:39:08,278 --> 00:39:09,215
(There it is…)

590
00:39:09,619 --> 00:39:12,193
(The life that is like a star
we make ourselves.)

591
00:39:12,563 --> 00:39:13,848
(Just like Cheewa said.)

592
00:39:15,120 --> 00:39:17,784
(Everything is a bit of a mess)

593
00:39:17,966 --> 00:39:20,327
(and out of plan.)

594
00:39:20,912 --> 00:39:23,832
(Last time, it was my mother
who got remarried.)

595
00:39:24,684 --> 00:39:28,596
(Years later, my dad got
remarried today, too.)

596
00:39:30,009 --> 00:39:34,766
(My two beloved stars are
having the time of their lives.)

597
00:39:35,694 --> 00:39:39,536
(Whose wedding would it be in the future…)

598
00:39:40,929 --> 00:39:41,992
(I can’t imagine it.)

599
00:39:46,197 --> 00:39:47,563
(As for my friends,)

600
00:39:48,330 --> 00:39:50,647
(they are all making their own stars.)

601
00:39:55,693 --> 00:39:56,773
(Thara…)

602
00:39:59,377 --> 00:40:02,796
(became a lawyer after finishing law school.)

603
00:40:04,572 --> 00:40:08,072
(Thipok released several singles,)

604
00:40:09,687 --> 00:40:11,834
(just like he dreamed of
when we were students.)

605
00:40:15,447 --> 00:40:18,148
(And the world-class blonde guitarist?)

606
00:40:18,684 --> 00:40:21,863
(Hem just suddenly got a wake-up call
from the ocean,)

607
00:40:22,045 --> 00:40:25,241
(falling in love with the scent and
the sound of waves hitting the shores.)

608
00:40:26,533 --> 00:40:30,673
(Jomyut talked his way
into starting a podcast,)

609
00:40:30,814 --> 00:40:32,516
(entertaining people about astronomy.)

610
00:40:33,344 --> 00:40:34,610
(It suits him, really.)

611
00:40:35,841 --> 00:40:39,280
(Newton became a full-time photographer)

612
00:40:39,522 --> 00:40:42,859
(despite his entrance exam score being
one of the country’s top scores.)

613
00:40:43,182 --> 00:40:46,036
(They’re so insane, these former nerds.)

614
00:40:47,671 --> 00:40:51,033
(As for my most important person
in the universe,)

615
00:40:53,152 --> 00:40:55,823
(I’m sure he will one day
become an astronaut.)

616
00:40:56,025 --> 00:41:00,735
(He said he had to know how to assemble
a spaceship before he could ride one.)

617
00:41:00,735 --> 00:41:05,635
PARNCHEEWA
(So Cheewa got into Astrospace Engineering.)

618
00:41:08,645 --> 00:41:09,696
(As for me,)

619
00:41:10,220 --> 00:41:12,184
(I decided to keep playing judo.)

620
00:41:12,184 --> 00:41:12,684
Come on.

621
00:41:12,684 --> 00:41:14,562
(I know now that I can never hate it.)

622
00:41:14,562 --> 00:41:15,078
Ready.

623
00:41:15,078 --> 00:41:15,778
Okay.

624
00:41:15,778 --> 00:41:19,259
(Actually, I really love it
and I’m so proud of it.)

625
00:41:19,542 --> 00:41:21,751
(I decided to get into university
a year later than my friends.)

626
00:41:21,751 --> 00:41:22,390
- You got this?
- Yes.

627
00:41:22,390 --> 00:41:25,371
(I trained so hard to get
into the national team.)

628
00:41:30,861 --> 00:41:32,642
(My joy during tournament...)

629
00:41:36,401 --> 00:41:38,272
PIANGNIRAN

630
00:41:38,272 --> 00:41:40,048
PIANGNIRAN
DO YOUR BEST

631
00:41:41,420 --> 00:41:43,010
(I gained it back.)

632
00:41:44,304 --> 00:41:46,215
PIANGNIRAN
DO YOUR BEST

633
00:41:49,803 --> 00:41:54,721
PIANGNIRAN

634
00:41:57,156 --> 00:42:01,585
If you believe in yourself,
victory will be yours one day.

635
00:42:41,452 --> 00:42:43,473
(Taking a year off of studying)

636
00:42:44,846 --> 00:42:48,267
(means I got into university
the same year as Cheewa.)

637
00:42:49,256 --> 00:42:53,265
(I got into Sport Science
on my judo scholarship.)

638
00:42:53,568 --> 00:42:55,781
(Our faculties are next to each other.)

639
00:42:59,010 --> 00:43:00,604
(We just stay together like this.)

640
00:43:01,008 --> 00:43:02,058
(It makes us happy.)

641
00:43:02,805 --> 00:43:04,914
(We’re still happy now.)

642
00:43:06,246 --> 00:43:08,322
(Everything is the same.)

643
00:43:08,605 --> 00:43:12,798
- (The world turns slowly in our own way.)
- You done with class?

644
00:43:13,504 --> 00:43:15,313
(Cheewa still asks me
all the same questions…)

645
00:43:15,454 --> 00:43:16,206
Alright. Let’s go home.

646
00:43:16,206 --> 00:43:20,048
(“Did you know this..?” and
“Did you know that..?”)

647
00:43:20,230 --> 00:43:20,730
Let’s go.

648
00:43:20,730 --> 00:43:23,531
(He still has stories
about the universe to tell me.)

649
00:43:23,531 --> 00:43:24,360
I’m still sleepy.

650
00:43:24,360 --> 00:43:25,932
(And I still want to hear everything.)

651
00:43:26,820 --> 00:43:28,786
(As long as it’s Cheewa
telling me these stories,)

652
00:43:29,634 --> 00:43:31,326
(as long as we’re still together,)

653
00:43:32,355 --> 00:43:37,378
(I’m happy to take a journey to any faraway
universe he wants to take me to.)

654
00:43:39,316 --> 00:43:43,512
(But my favorite place is no planet or star.)

655
00:43:44,017 --> 00:43:46,495
(It’s this same old tiny earth.)

656
00:43:47,161 --> 00:43:50,457
(I wish the world would stop
turning right now.)

657
00:43:50,639 --> 00:43:56,120
(But if the world stops turning,
everyone will die, like Cheewa said.)

658
00:43:56,120 --> 00:43:57,188
(Well, then…)

659
00:43:57,592 --> 00:44:00,057
(Since we’re all going to die soon,)

660
00:44:01,571 --> 00:44:04,120
(a goodnight kiss wouldn’t hurt.)

661
00:44:31,710 --> 00:44:32,638
(Ah…)

662
00:44:32,900 --> 00:44:36,034
(The world stopped turning,
and we didn’t die.)

663
00:44:36,397 --> 00:44:40,441
(But I’d die if I didn’t kiss Cheewa.)

664
00:45:09,703 --> 00:45:11,079
(You guys watching this…)

665
00:45:12,956 --> 00:45:15,201
(Do you have a Cheewa of your own?)

666
00:45:21,902 --> 00:45:25,521
If I want our wedding to be on Mars…

667
00:45:26,046 --> 00:45:27,052
Would you go there?

668
00:45:27,516 --> 00:45:28,560
I’m not in the frame at all?

669
00:45:28,843 --> 00:45:29,609
(Not at all.)

670
00:45:29,609 --> 00:45:30,190
Alright.

671
00:45:30,190 --> 00:45:31,457
Now that’s what I wanna hear.

672
00:45:31,457 --> 00:45:32,284
HE WALKS AWAY.

673
00:45:32,566 --> 00:45:33,245
Blackout?

674
00:45:33,245 --> 00:45:33,745
(Yes.)

675
00:45:33,745 --> 00:45:34,245
Every time!

676
00:45:34,386 --> 00:45:36,378
WE ALMOST GOT TO GO HOME EARLY.
It happens every time during the last scene!

677
00:45:36,684 --> 00:45:37,845
(Shall we start again from the top?)

678
00:45:38,067 --> 00:45:38,898
No.

679
00:45:40,444 --> 00:45:41,077
(Cut.)

680
00:45:41,077 --> 00:45:41,891
(Cut.)

681
00:45:42,684 --> 00:45:43,861
GIVE ME THE CLIPPERBOARD!

682
00:45:43,861 --> 00:45:44,919
WHERE’S THE CLIPPERBOARD?
I’LL USE IT MYSELF!

683
00:45:44,919 --> 00:45:45,835
Come on, guys.

684
00:45:45,835 --> 00:45:47,374
LET ME HELP PACK UP.

685
00:45:53,449 --> 00:45:54,295
Yes.

686
00:45:54,860 --> 00:45:55,618
Yes.

687
00:45:55,618 --> 00:45:56,725
But your arms…

688
00:45:57,359 --> 00:45:58,455
Yes! That’s it!

689
00:46:08,658 --> 00:46:11,503
(Twist… Twist your knee.)

690
00:46:12,342 --> 00:46:13,554
(Let’s get a professional to help.)

691
00:46:13,554 --> 00:46:15,287
DON’T TRY IT YOURSELVES, GUYS.

692
00:46:16,215 --> 00:46:17,325
The biggest one.

693
00:46:17,406 --> 00:46:18,703
Where’s mine?

694
00:46:18,905 --> 00:46:20,254
ONLOOKER 1/ONLOOKER 2

695
00:46:20,254 --> 00:46:21,012
You want a heart?

696
00:46:22,067 --> 00:46:22,868
(Okay. Cut.)

697
00:46:22,868 --> 00:46:23,682
(Cut.)

698
00:46:24,207 --> 00:46:25,267
Why don’t you go and ask him?

699
00:46:25,267 --> 00:46:26,196
WHY CAN’T I ASK YOU?

700
00:46:34,556 --> 00:46:35,403
How did you slick your hair back just now?

701
00:46:40,045 --> 00:46:40,936
Well…

702
00:46:41,661 --> 00:46:43,184
AM I HANDSOME?
Well…

703
00:46:43,184 --> 00:46:44,738
“Do you like singers?”

704
00:46:46,211 --> 00:46:46,998
Answer!

705
00:46:46,998 --> 00:46:51,721
I LIKE YOU.

706
00:46:51,721 --> 00:46:52,778
Bye-bye.

707
00:46:56,171 --> 00:46:57,711
One, two, three.

708
00:47:00,516 --> 00:47:01,814
That’s a wrap!

709
00:47:01,814 --> 00:47:02,985
It’s a wrap!

710
00:47:03,207 --> 00:47:04,953
It’s finally a wrap!

711
00:47:04,953 --> 00:47:07,574
Let’s throw Keen in the water!
